de the sandbox, Codex would try to write to `/tmp/khome-XXXXXX/.codex`, which is fine.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the sandbox profile:\n- It denies file-read-data and file-write* for subpaths of HOME (the real home)\n- It allows file-read-data and file-write* for `~/.kimi-code` (which is under the real home)\n\nFor Codex, we might need similar allowances. But since we're setting HOME to a scratch directory, and the Codex binary is at `/opt/homebrew/bin/codex` (not under HOME), it should work. The sandbox profile doesn't deny access to `/opt/homebrew` or `/tmp`.\n\nLet me update the sandbox profile to also allow Codex's typical directories. Looking at common Codex installations, it might use `~/.codex` or the Homebrew cellar. Let me add a general allowance for the Homebrew prefix:"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
